---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, SOCIALS } from '../consts';
import { withBase } from '../utils/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description={`About ${SITE.title} and its author, ${SITE.author}.`}
  path="/about"
  narrow
>
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

  <div class="prose about">
    <p>
      <strong>{SITE.title}</strong> is a working notebook kept in public. It covers AI and LLM systems,
      web engineering, and the infrastructure that has to keep both of them up.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every post here follows the same rules, because they are the rules that make a technical post
      worth the reading time:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Show the mechanism.</strong> Diagrams, charts and measured numbers, not adjectives. If
        a claim can be plotted, it gets plotted.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Name the trade-off.</strong> Every technique costs something. A post that only lists
        benefits is advertising.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cite the source.</strong> Each post ends with links to the documentation, papers and
        benchmarks it leans on — so you can check the work rather than trust it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>

    <p>
      Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, styled with Tailwind CSS, diagrams by
      Mermaid, charts by Chart.js, search by Pagefind. Deployed to GitHub Pages from{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/sehyunnoh/techblog">sehyunnoh/techblog</a>. The chart palette is
      validated for colour-vision deficiency in both light and dark themes, and every chart ships a
      data table alongside it.
    </p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>

    <ul>
      {SOCIALS.map((s) => <li><a href={s.href} rel="me noopener">{s.label}</a></li>)}
      <li><a href={withBase('/rss.xml')}>RSS feed</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    font-weight: 680;
  }

  .about {
    max-width: none;
  }
</style>
